speechtext:
I will admit that many of them are not competent. Speaking of incompetence, let us go back to subsection (a), which reads:
-employs a person ait a rate of wages less than the minimum wage rate fixed by law or any competent public authority;
During the investigation we found cases in which the minimum wage law had to be

Criminal Code Amendment
ignored, and this was particularly so in the garment trades. As I said before the public had ceased to buy garments; they could not buy them. What were they doing? The women had sewing machines in their homes, and they were commencing to make their own garments. Those engaged in the garment trades, therefore, had to compete with the housewives who had sewing machines in their homes. That is why wages are always low in the garment trades; they have to compete with the housewives. As I have already said, it was found that people would not buy garments at the prices which the factories had to charge. Then, by agreement between the employers, the employees and the unions, they said, ''In order to get work at all in these factories we will have to take wages less than those provided by the minimum wage law." We asked the competent authority of one of the provinces how he arrived at his minimum wage. He replied, "Oh, we arrived at that fifteen years ago. WTe based it on the cost of living." Then he was asked, "Have you never Changed it since?" He replied, "No, there has been no change in the cost of living since then, so we never bothered changing the law." He was so competent that he did not know that in the last fifteen years the cost of living has varied as much as twenty per cent, but the minimum' wage had not been varied accordingly. Now let us look at the next offence:
(c)	falsifies any employment record required to be kept by law or any competent public authority;
Have we not laws already against falsifying records? I think we have, so we do not need further laws. Then the next offence:
(d)	punches a time clock with intent to deceive;
Is there not a law against that now? It is the same as making a false entry in a record. Then let us turn to the next offence:
(e)	puts the wages of more than one employee in the same envelope with intent to evade the provisions of any minimum wage law;
Any person wishing to evade that section simply need not use envelopes. The offence is putting the wages in an envelope.
